Using the :attr:`dim` argument to compute matrix norms::

    >>> A = torch.arange(8, dtype=torch.float).reshape(2, 2, 2)
    >>> LA.norm(A, dim=(1,2))
    tensor([ 3.7417, 11.2250])
    >>> LA.norm(A[0, :, :]), LA.norm(A[1, :, :])
    (tensor(3.7417), tensor(11.2250))

