        For example, `torch.linalg.norm(A, ord=1, dim=(0, 1))` always
        computes a matrix norm, but with `torch.linalg.vector_norm(A, ord=1, dim=(0, 1))` it is possible
        to compute a vector norm over the two dimensions.

